.page ntpdate 1 set the clock from an NTP server

# SYNOPSIS
*ntpdate* [*-qw*] [*-p* _PORT_] [*-t* _SECONDS_] _SERVER_

# DESCRIPTION
`ntpdate` asks the NTP server once and steps the system clock to its time; it is `sntp -s`. `-w` writes the clock chip too, `-q` only asks. Setting the clock needs root. Read `sntp(1)` for the details of the exchange, the options and the time zone question.

# EXAMPLES
    ntpdate 10.0.2.2
    ntpdate -w ntp.example.test

# SEE ALSO
sntp(1), hwclock(8), clock(7)
